{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-11-05_aap-ex99_1.htm, sha256 24569e95b2ca1df25af4f15fefba70e3807f2d0f62c10f2607ef01b6e38a70cc.\nEX-99.1 2 aap-ex99_1.htm EX-99.1\nExhibit 99.1\nAdvance Auto Parts Reports Third Quarter 2026 Results; Updates Full Year 2026 Guidance\nl Comparable Sales Trends Improved Sequentially During Q3 2026; Turned Positive In the Final Four Weeks\nl FY 2026 Free Cash Flow Guidance Raised To Approx. $150 Million; Over $400 Million Growth Year-over-Year\nRALEIGH, N.C., November 5, 2026 \u2014 Advance Auto Parts, Inc. (NYSE: AAP), a leading automotive aftermarket parts provider in North America, that serves both professional installer and do-it-yourself customers, announced its financial results for the third quarter ended October 10, 2026.\n\"Our comparable sales performance improved as the quarter progressed. Main Street Pro outperformed throughout the quarter while DIY trends improved compared to the softer trends experienced during the summer. I thank the team for their hard work and commitment to serving our customers,\" said Shane O'Kelly, president and chief executive officer. \"Sales declined in the low-single-digit range during the first eight weeks before turning positive in the final four weeks, supported by improved transaction volumes. The Pro channel led performance in Q3, with low-single-digit sales growth including stronger Main Street Pro growth. The DIY channel declined in the low-single-digit range for the quarter, with trends recovering from negative mid-single-digit levels at the start of the quarter. Despite the volatile demand environment and industry cost pressures, we delivered an adjusted operating margin of 4.5% in Q3 and generated over $100 million of free cash flow year-to-date. We believe that our strategic initiatives are starting to gain traction and we remain focused on delivering sustainable, profitable growth over the long term.\"\nThird Quarter 2026 Results (1)\nThird quarter 2026 net sales totaled $2,012 million, compared with $2,036 million in the third quarter of the prior year. Comparable store sales for the third quarter 2026 decreased 1.2%.\nThe Company's third quarter 2026 gross profit was $897 million, or 44.6% of net sales compared with $881 million, or 43.3% in the third quarter of 2025. Adjusted gross profit was $899 million, or 44.7% of net sales in the third quarter of 2026 compared with $913 million, or 44.8% in the third quarter of 2025. The decrease in gross profit as a percentage of net sales compared to the third quarter of 2025 was primarily driven by changes in product and channel sales mix compared to last year and supply chain expense deleverage.\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "The Company's third quarter 2026 selling, general and administrative (SG&A) expenses were $850 million, or 42.2% of net sales compared with $859 million, or 42.2% of net sales in the third quarter of 2025. Adjusted SG&A expenses were $808 million, or 40.2% of net sales in the third quarter of 2026 compared with $823 million, or 40.4% of net sales in the third quarter of 2025. The decrease in SG&A as a percentage of net sales compared to the third quarter of 2025 was primarily driven by a reduction in expenses compared to last year, supported by disciplined expense management.\nThe Company's third quarter 2026 operating income was $47 million, or 2.3% of net sales, compared with $22 million, or 1.1% of net sales in the third quarter of 2025. Adjusted operating income was $91 million or 4.5% of net sales in the third quarter of 2026, compared with $90 million or 4.4% of net sales in the third quarter of 2025.\nThe Company's third quarter 2026 diluted earnings per share was $0.25, compared with loss of $0.02 in the third quarter of 2025. Adjusted diluted earnings per share was $0.79 in the third quarter of 2026, compared with $0.92 in the third quarter of 2025.\n(1) The Company calculates comparable store sales based on the change in store sales starting once a location has been open for approximately one year and by including e-commerce sales and excluding sales fulfilled by distribution centers to independently owned Carquest locations. The Company includes sales from relocated stores in comparable store sales from the original date of opening. Closed stores are not included in the comparable store sales calculation. Comparable store sales is intended only as supplemental information and is not a substitute for Net sales presented in accordance with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (\"GAAP\").\nCapital Allocation\nOn October 26, 2026, the Company declared a regular cash dividend of $0.25 per share to be paid on January 22, 2027 to all common stockholders of record as of January 8, 2027.\nFull Year 2026 Guidance(1)\nThe Company has revised its full year 2026 guidance to reflect year-to-date financial performance and updated operating assumptions for the fourth quarter of 2026.\nAs of November 5, 2026\nPrior Guidance\n($ in millions, except per share data)\nLow\nHigh\nLow\nHigh\nNet sales\nApprox.$8,500\n$8,485\n$8,575\nComparable store sales (52 weeks)(2)\nApprox. 1.00%\n1.00%\n2.00%\nAdjusted operating income margin\n4.00%\n4.30%\n3.80%\n4.50%\nAdjusted diluted EPS(3)\n$2.75\n$3.10\n$2.60\n$3.30\nCapital expenditures\nApprox. $300\nApprox. $300\nFree cash flow\nApprox. $150\nApprox. $100\nStore growth\nNew store openings\n30 - 35\n30 - 35\nMarket hub openings\n15 - 20\n15 - 20\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "(1) Adjusted operating income margin, Adjusted diluted EPS and Free cash flow are Non-GAAP measures. For a better understanding of the Company's Non-GAAP adjustments, refer to the reconciliation of Non-GAAP financial measures in the accompanying financial tables. The Company is not able to provide a reconciliation of these forward-looking Non-GAAP measures presented herein because it is unable to predict with reasonable accuracy the value of certain adjustments and as a result, the comparable GAAP measures are unavailable without unreasonable efforts. (2) Comparable store sales for fiscal 2026 is calculated based on an adjusted fiscal 2025 baseline to account for the 53rd week. The Company calculates comparable store sales based on the change in store sales starting once a location has been open for approximately one year and by including e-commerce sales and excluding sales fulfilled by distribution centers to independently owned Carquest locations. The Company includes sales from relocated stores in comparable store sales from the original date of opening. Comparable store sales is intended only as supplemental information and is not a substitute for Net sales presented in accordance with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (\u201cGAAP\u201d). (3) Includes pre-tax interest expense of approximately $210 million and pre-tax interest income of approximately $105 million.\nInvestor Conference Call\nThe Company will detail its results for the third quarter and full year 2026 via a webcast scheduled to begin at 8 a.m. Eastern Time on Thursday, November 5, 2026. The webcast will be accessible via the Investor Relations page of the Company's website (ir.AdvanceAutoParts.com).\nTo join by phone, please pre-register online for dial-in and passcode information. While registration is open through the live call, the Company suggests registering a minimum 10 minutes before the start of the call. A replay of the conference call will be available on the Company's Investor Relations website for one year.\nAbout Advance Auto Parts\nAdvance Auto Parts, Inc. is a leading automotive aftermarket parts provider that serves both professional installers and do-it-yourself customers. As of October 10, 2026, Advance operated 4,325 stores primarily within the United States, with additional locations in Canada, Puerto Rico and the U.S. Virgin Islands. The Company also served 787 independently owned Carquest branded stores across these locations in addition to various Caribbean islands. Additional information about Advance, including employment opportunities, customer services, and online shopping for parts, accessories and other offerings can be found at www.AdvanceAutoParts.com.\nInvestor Relations Contact:\nMedia Contact:\nLavesh Hemnani\nNicole Ducouer\nE: invrelations@advance-auto.com\nE: AAPcommunications@advance-auto.com\nForward-Looking Statements\n"}
